                    <p>AD Code Registration in Delhi is the mandatory process of obtaining a 14-digit Authorized Dealer Code from your RBI-authorized bank and registering it on ICEGATE (icegate.gov.in) for Delhi's customs ports - IGI Air Customs (INDEL4), ICD Tughlakabad (INTKD6), or ICD Okhla. Requires IEC from DGFT. One-time registration; lifetime validity; no government fee. <a href="/ad-code-registration">Learn more about AD Code Registration across India</a>.</p>
                </div>
                <p>Delhi exports flow through three customs channels: IGI Airport air cargo, ICD Tughlakabad rail containers to JNPT (India's largest dry port), and ICD Okhla. Every Delhi exporter must register AD Code at the correct port on ICEGATE.</p>
                <p>The DGFT Delhi Regional Office at Udyog Bhawan issues the IEC that is the mandatory pre-requisite for AD Code. Patron runs IEC and AD Code as a concurrent workflow, eliminating weeks of serial delay. For IEC, see <a href="/iec-registration">IEC Registration</a>. For GST compliance, see <a href="/gst-registration">GST Registration</a>.</p>
