<!-- SECTION 3: WHAT IS GSTAT APPEAL FILING -->
<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is AD Code Registration?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>AD Code Registration is the mandatory one-time process of obtaining a 14-digit Authorized Dealer Code from an RBI-authorized bank branch and registering it on the ICEGATE portal (icegate.gov.in) for the specific customs port, enabling shipping bill generation, FEMA-compliant foreign exchange receipts, and direct credit of export incentives like RoDTEP, Duty Drawback, and IGST refunds.</p>
                    <p>Every export requires three linked registrations: (1) IEC from DGFT - the exporter's identity; (2) AD Code from your bank - linking IEC to your bank account; (3) ICEGATE registration - linking AD Code to the customs port. These are sequential: IEC first, then AD Code letter, then ICEGATE registration. Patron manages all three as a single integrated workflow for Delhi exporters.</p>
                    <p>Under FEMA 1999, the AD Code links every shipping bill to the RBI-authorized dealer bank through which export proceeds must flow. RBI monitors through EDPMS/IDPMS systems. A wrong or unregistered AD Code disrupts FEMA tracking and can expose the exporter to RBI queries. For company formation before exporting, see <a href="/private-limited-company-registration">Company Registration</a>.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for AD Code Registration in Delhi:</strong></p>
                    <p><strong>AD Code:</strong> 14-digit number from RBI-authorized bank branch on letterhead in DGFT-prescribed format. Uniquely identifies the bank branch for export forex transactions.</p><p><strong>IEC:</strong> 10-digit Import Export Code from DGFT - mandatory pre-requisite. DGFT Delhi Regional Office at Udyog Bhawan issues IEC for Delhi businesses.</p><p><strong>ICEGATE:</strong> Indian Customs Electronic Gateway (icegate.gov.in) - national digital customs platform. All shipping bills filed here. AD Code registration done under "Bank Account Management."</p><p><strong>CBIC PN 93/2020:</strong> Single-port AD Code rule - register at one port, reflects at all others. BUT IFSC for incentives must be registered port-wise separately.</p><p><strong>EDPMS/IDPMS:</strong> RBI systems tracking export/import transactions via AD Code. Every shipping bill generates an EDPMS entry linked to the exporter's AD Code.</p>

                </div>
            </div>
