<section class="content-section" id="who-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Who Needs AD Code Registration in Delhi?</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <p>Karol Bagh is Delhi's most concentrated garment export cluster. Hundreds of manufacturers and trading houses export apparel to US, EU, Middle East. AD Code at IGI Air Customs (INDEL4) is critical - most apparel exports move by air through IGI Airport's Air Cargo Complex. RoDTEP credits (1-4% of FOB value) are credited to the AD Code-linked bank account.</p>
                <p>Chandni Chowk - Old Delhi's historic trading district - is the heart of handicraft, jewellery, spices, and textile exports. Most Chandni Chowk exporters use ICD Tughlakabad (INTKD6) for sea freight via CONCOR's daily rail containers to JNPT Mumbai - more cost-effective than road transport. ICD Tughlakabad, commissioned 1993, is India's largest dry port by volume.</p>
                <p>Nehru Place and Connaught Place IT/software companies represent a significant AD Code audience - software exporters receiving foreign exchange remittances need FEMA compliance under EDPMS. Okhla, Bawana, and Narela manufacturers who ship containers use Tughlakabad as their primary customs and stuffing point. E-commerce MSME exporters use IGI Airport courier services.</p>

            </div>
