<section class="content-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="text-content">
            <h2 class="section-title">Legal Framework for AD Code Registration in Delhi</h2>
            <div class="content-text">
                
                <ul><li><strong>FEMA 1999:</strong> All export proceeds must be repatriated through RBI-authorized channels. AD Code links shipping bills to the specific AD bank for EDPMS monitoring. <a href="https://icegate.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ICEGATE Portal</a></li><li><strong>FT(D&R) Act 1992:</strong> Governs foreign trade policy. DGFT issues IEC under this Act. AD Code is in DGFT-approved format. <a href="https://dgft.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">DGFT Portal</a></li><li><strong>ICEGATE (icegate.gov.in):</strong> CBIC's national digital customs platform. Shipping bills, Bills of Entry all filed here. AD Code mandatory pre-requisite for shipping bill generation.</li><li><strong>CBIC PN 93/2020:</strong> Single-port AD Code rule. Register at one port, reflects at all others. BUT IFSC must still be registered port-wise for incentive payments. <a href="https://delhicustoms.gov.in" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Delhi Customs</a></li><li><strong>EDPMS/IDPMS:</strong> RBI export/import monitoring systems. Every shipping bill generates an EDPMS entry linked to AD Code. Wrong AD Code = FEMA compliance queries.</li><li><strong>ICD Tughlakabad (INTKD6):</strong> India's largest dry port. CONCOR flagship terminal commissioned 1993. Daily rail to JNPT Mumbai. Port code INTKD6 on ICEGATE.</li></ul>

            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</section>

