                <div class="faq-expanded__list">
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-1">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What is an AD Code and why do I need it to export from Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>AD Code (Authorized Dealer Code) is a 14-digit number from your RBI-authorized bank on letterhead, registered on ICEGATE for your customs port. Without it, ICEGATE will not allow shipping bill generation - no goods can ship from IGI Air Customs (INDEL4), ICD Tughlakabad (INTKD6), or ICD Okhla. Also required for RoDTEP, Duty Drawback, and IGST refund credits to reach your bank account.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-2">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How do I get an AD Code letter from my bank in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Write formal letter to Branch Manager of your RBI-authorized Category-I AD bank (SBI, PNB, HDFC, ICICI, Axis). Request AD Code mentioning IEC number and Delhi port (INDEL4 for IGI Airport or INTKD6 for Tughlakabad). Submit with IEC certificate, PAN, GST, cancelled cheque. Bank issues 14-digit code on letterhead in 1-3 working days. Name/address must exactly match IEC to avoid ICEGATE rejection.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-3">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Which ports require AD Code registration in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Three main ports: (1) IGI Air Customs INDEL4 for air cargo; (2) ICD Tughlakabad INTKD6 for sea freight via CONCOR rail to JNPT - India's largest dry port; (3) ICD Okhla for South Delhi. Per CBIC PN 93/2020, register at ONE port, reflects at all others. But IFSC for Duty Drawback/IGST refunds must be registered port-wise separately at each Delhi port - Patron includes this as standard.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-4">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How do I register AD Code on ICEGATE?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Register on ICEGATE 2.0 (icegate.gov.in) as IEC holder with Class 3 DSC. Upload documents via eSanchit - receive DRN/IRN. Navigate to Financial Services > Bank Account Management > AD Code Registration. Select Delhi port (INDEL4 or INTKD6), enter AD Code and IRN, complete OTP, submit. Customs approval in 3-4 working days. Separately register IFSC port-wise for incentive payments.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-5">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">What documents are required for AD Code registration?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>AD Code letter from bank on letterhead; IEC certificate from DGFT; company PAN card; GST certificate; cancelled cheque; authorization letter/board resolution for companies; Class 3 DSC for ICEGATE; exporter's letter to Customs Commissioner at specific Delhi port. All names, addresses, PAN must be exactly consistent across all documents - any mismatch causes rejection.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-6">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">How long does AD Code registration take in Delhi?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>7-12 working days total: bank letter 1-3 days; ICEGATE setup 1-2 days; customs approval 3-4 days; IFSC registration 1-2 days (parallel). If rejected for name mismatch: 15-25 days. Patron's pre-check prevents rejections. Express service available for first-shipment urgency.</p></div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="faq-expanded__item" id="faq-7">
                        <h3 class="faq-expanded__q">Can I register AD Code at multiple Delhi ports?</h3>
                        <div class="faq-expanded__a"><p>Per CBIC PN 93/2020, register at one port and it reflects at all others. So registering at IGI (INDEL4) makes AD Code available at Tughlakabad (INTKD6) and Okhla too. However, IFSC for Duty Drawback/IGST/RoDTEP credits must be registered separately at each Delhi port under Bank Account Export Promotion Incentive on ICEGATE. Patron registers IFSC at all ports as standard.</p></div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>


